/designs                       /portal.html   200
/pipelines                     /portal.html   200

# ── EVERY OLD /portal ADDRESS, PERMANENTLY, TO ITS ROOT FORM ──────────────────────────────
# /portal/<page>[/<sub>] was the app's address from 2026-07-29 to 2026-10-13, and those links
# live on in emails already sent (orders, password resets, invites), the phone apps' "Open in
# Structure Studio", bookmarks and the installed app. The query string rides along (the host
# keeps the request's own when the target names none), so ?view=<builder> operator links and a
# reset link's ?code= arrive whole; a #fragment never reaches the host and the browser keeps it
# across the redirect. ssRootPath in portal/01-core.jsx makes the same mapping in the browser.
#
# Bare /portal and /portal/ are the sign-in form, /login (the splat rule below would send
# /portal/ to `/`, the designer, so both are spelled out). /portal/admin was the Admin page.
/portal                        /login         301
/portal/                       /login         301
/portal/admin                  /console       301

